==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{q|verb}} {{IPA|en|/ɪˈnɪʃ.i.eɪt/|/ɪˈnɪʃ.ɪ.eɪt/}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-initiate.wav|a=Southern England}}
** {{rhymes|en|ɪʃieɪt|s=4}}
* {{q|noun|adjective}} {{IPA|en|/ɪˈnɪʃ.i.ət/|/ɪˈnɪʃ.ɪ.ət/}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-initiate2.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{hyphenation|en|ini|ti|ate}}

===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*h₁ey-}}
{{bor+|en|la|initiātus}}, {{glossary|perfect}} {{glossary|passive}} {{glossary|participle}} of {{m|la|initiō||to begin, originate}} (see {{af|en|-ate|id1=verb|pos1=verb-forming suffix}}), from {{m|la|initium||a beginning}} + {{m|la|-ō|id=denominative|pos=verb-forming suffix}}, from {{m|la|initus||an entrance, coming in, approach}} + {{m|la|-ium}}, from {{m|la|ineō}} + {{m|la|-tus|id=action noun}}, from {{m|la|in-|id=in}} + {{m|la|eō||to go}}. Cognate with {{cog|fr|initier}}.

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[begin]]; to [[start]].
#* {{RQ:Isaac Taylor Ultimate Civilization|passage=How are changes of this sort to be '''initiated'''?}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1978|author=David Dhlalangami Maforo|title=Black-white Relations in Kenya Game Policy|page=5
|passage=Indigenous people, such as agriculturists, hunters, and pastoralists '''initiated''' a system of totemism and tabooism which in essence was a natural law against killing and eating certain animals.}}
#* {{quote-book|en
|year=2011
|title=The First War of Physics
|author=Jim Baggott
|publisher=Pegasus Books
|isbn=9781605987699
|passage=A U235 bomb would therefore need to incorporate a gun weighing ten tons. Then there was the question of '''initiating''' or triggering the bomb.
}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2014|author=David L. Elliott|title=Ultraviolet Laser Technology and Applications|page=320
|passage=Prior to firing the laser, a surgeon can preilluminate the area to be cut or ablated, enlarge or reduce the area, shape, or size, and then '''initiate''' the UV laser pulses for the actual ablation.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[instruct]] in the [[rudiment]]s or [[principle]]s; to [[introduce]].
#: {{syn|en|induct}}
#* {{RQ:More Antidote|passage=Divine Providence would only initiate and enter mankind into the useful knowledge of her, leaving the rest to employ our industry.}}
#* {{RQ:Locke Education|94
|passage=to '''initiate''' his pupil in any part of learning}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[confer]] [[membership]] on; especially, to admit to a secret order with mysterious rites or ceremonies.
#* {{RQ:Warburton Divine Legation|passage=The Athenians believed that he who was '''initiated''' and instructed in the mysteries would obtain celestial honour after death.}}
#* {{RQ:Spectator|VI|576|August 4 1714|author=Addison|passage=He was '''initiated''' into half a dozen clubs before he was one and twenty.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To do the first act; to perform the first rite; to take the initiative.
#* {{RQ:Homer Pope et al Odyssey|3|passage=The king himself '''initiates''' to the power; Scatters with quivering hand the sacred flour, And the stream sprinkles.}}

=====Synonyms=====
