===Etymology 2===
From a [[substantivization]] of the [[adjective]], see {{af|en|-ate|id1=substantive|pos1=noun-forming suffix}} and [[#Etymology 1|Etymology 1]] for more. Cognate with {{cog|fr|initié||an initiate, neophyte}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{senseid|en|new member of an organization}} A new [[member]] of an organization.
# {{senseid|en|one who has been through a ceremony of initiation}} One who has been through a ceremony of [[initiation]].<!--Often coinstantial with the first sense.-->
# {{senseid|en|one who is knowledgeable and experienced in a topic}} One who is {{l|en|oriented#Adjective}} in and {{l|en|familiar#Adjective}} with a topic or subject; especially, one who is an {{l|en|expert#Noun}} in it.
#: {{ant|en|noninitiate#Noun|novice#Noun}}
#: {{cot|en|expert#Noun|nonexpert#Noun|;|layperson|amateur#Noun|dilettante|;|insider|old hand|;|journeyman|master#Noun|;|learner|student|teacher}}<!--Because of the semantic breadth of ""initiate" [noun], all of these can overlap with it.-->

